  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The hydrogen attached with most electronegative carbon will be the most acidic.</p><p>The hydrogen, attached with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sp</mi></math>-hybrid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>-atom is most acidic because of highest electronegativity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sp</mi></math> hybrid carbon atom, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> atom becomes relatively more acidic.</p>",
